From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] DPP: require a PMKSA of the DPP AKM before skipping Network
 Introduction

wpas_dpp_check_connect() skips the Network Introduction protocol when
wpa_sm_pmksa_exists() finds a PMKSA for the BSS. That lookup ignores the
AKM, so a PMKSA from an SAE association, made while the AP did not offer
the DPP AKM, counts as one for DPP. Once the AP offers DPP again, the
station associates with the DPP AKM without a PMKID, and the AP rejects
the Association Request with status 53 (invalid PMKID), because
wpa_validate_wpa_ie() requires a PMKSA for DPP.

Look up a PMKSA of the DPP AKM instead. For an AP MLD, also require the
entry under the AP MLD address, which is the one an MLD association looks
up and which the Peer Discovery Response handler stores beside the
per-link entry.

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---

--- a/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/dpp_supplicant.c
@@ -4564,6 +4564,23 @@ static int wpas_dpp_start_private_peer_i
 #endif /* CONFIG_DPP3 */
 
 
+static bool wpas_dpp_pmksa_exists(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s,
+				  struct wpa_ssid *ssid, struct wpa_bss *bss)
+{
+	if (!wpa_sm_pmksa_cache_get(wpa_s->wpa, bss->bssid, NULL, ssid,
+				    WPA_KEY_MGMT_DPP))
+		return false;
+
+	/* An MLD association looks up the PMKSA by the AP MLD address. */
+	if (!is_zero_ether_addr(bss->mld_addr) &&
+	    !wpa_sm_pmksa_cache_get(wpa_s->wpa, bss->mld_addr, NULL, ssid,
+				    WPA_KEY_MGMT_DPP))
+		return false;
+
+	return true;
+}
+
+
 int wpas_dpp_check_connect(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s, struct wpa_ssid *ssid,
 			   struct wpa_bss *bss)
 {
@@ -4580,7 +4597,7 @@ int wpas_dpp_check_connect(struct wpa_su
 	if (rsn && wpa_parse_wpa_ie(rsn, 2 + rsn[1], &ied) == 0 &&
 	    !(ied.key_mgmt & WPA_KEY_MGMT_DPP))
 		return 0; /* AP does not support DPP AKM - continue */
-	if (wpa_sm_pmksa_exists(wpa_s->wpa, bss->bssid, wpa_s->own_addr, ssid))
+	if (wpas_dpp_pmksa_exists(wpa_s, ssid, bss))
 		return 0; /* PMKSA exists for DPP AKM - continue */
 
 	if (!ssid->dpp_connector || !ssid->dpp_netaccesskey ||
